# PHP / Sage 11 App Layer Conventions

## Namespace

All PHP in `app/` uses the `App` namespace:

```php
namespace App;
```

## Key files

| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `app/setup.php` | Theme support, WooCommerce wrappers, script/style enqueues |
| `app/filters.php` | WordPress filter hooks |
| `app/View/Composers/App.php` | Data shared across all views |
| `app/View/Composers/Post.php` | Data for single post/page views |

## Adding data to Blade views — use View Composers, not blade PHP blocks

```php
// app/View/Composers/App.php
public function with(): array
{
    return [
        'siteName' => get_bloginfo('name'),
    ];
}
```

## WooCommerce integration

- Theme support and wrapper removal: `app/setup.php`
- Shop/product/cart/checkout Blade wrapper: `resources/views/woocommerce.blade.php`
- "Coming soon" mode must be disabled: `wp option update woocommerce_coming_soon no`

## Asset URLs — always use the Vite facade

```php
use Illuminate\Support\Facades\Vite;

Vite::asset('resources/images/logo.svg');  // ✅
get_template_directory_uri() . '/public/build/...'  // ❌ hardcoded, breaks on hot reload
```

## PHP lint

```bash
./vendor/bin/pint --test   # check only
./vendor/bin/pint          # auto-fix
```
